ligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 13\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124540 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "823a7d28-5a92-5901-8ee0-e5116df6766b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Image of a Vector Given the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "599638fe-e3f5-5032-bcd9-5e38ff434df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324716} {:answer/id #uuid "5c8c5132-0247-532b-82f8-d1c35e84e006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324741} {:answer/id #uuid "5e626344-4849-53d2-89ed-44127837a74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324756} {:answer/id #uuid "c7eed510-5c26-552d-8faa-ae1d4def6c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325705} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e7297f-94f0-54b1-9633-d7cfea9f0980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "599638fe-e3f5-5032-bcd9-5e38ff434df2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324716} :answer-field/id #uuid "d37072c5-cb1a-5c0f-8693-59719072ef9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ade064ac-fc93-5e6f-a92b-aac7997b4ec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-38881" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$\\,$ $[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 11 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The image of $[x]_{B}$ relative to the basis $B$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 \\\\ 11 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Images of the Basis Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ae6f887-9034-5ef8-bbb3-73fcb564cbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324722} {:answer/id #uuid "b0370c89-3def-55f0-a581-30c0bbb04bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325471} {:answer/id #uuid "befd06fe-4449-5b38-b9fb-cf6fa14531dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325613} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd77663-15f8-5c3a-b608-64f1230c7341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325779} {:answer/id #uuid "dcbbf9ea-7d56-5bfe-ae44-a6a93391934e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ae6f887-9034-5ef8-bbb3-73fcb564cbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324722} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5c29b68-bad2-5f86-be29-ee7030d5ad62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f693b21-522a-541c-bcba-50ee0dfa8db7" :question/math-academy-id "q-38883" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})=8{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=7{b}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})=8{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=7{b}_{1}$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Images of the Basis Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203ae31f-e7d7-5ba9-985d-c5c53968ef9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392247} {:answer/id #uuid "d9505477-b80c-5e60-9ad5-b8cceaf69da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392248} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cd5bf-81b1-5350-b65a-736745d05714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392249} {:answer/id #uuid "4e43d5b8-d929-5ed6-8f43-093ad3710dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392250} {:answer/id #uuid "c1643dd1-1ac2-5766-b8de-dea684f1a01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cd5bf-81b1-5350-b65a-736745d05714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392249} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac46a3d-440c-54c6-a48d-2372df405d0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "217d7c6a-01fa-5c09-8fc9-462942a415a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-38884" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124541 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22ca4f81-6fec-5822-b281-5ce1e23d399e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Three-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85805c10-1fa7-52ba-afd2-327a0327b7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123459} {:answer/id #uuid "c1703cdd-330b-5be4-8dab-f3bf0b06d6f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123460} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b9a787-46f1-5b4c-90cb-b940e9b0337a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123461} {:answer/id #uuid "0e63182f-7289-5072-a966-40e1acf026a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123462} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd5195e-4df1-52ff-9462-50b896a4e077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123463}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3891a074-2c4f-5312-8060-b3161b129164" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123458} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa4e200d-3059-501b-ab48-6218a57adb56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366092} {:answer/id #uuid "07fc866b-fe6c-5b59-a12b-1c07c6f776d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366093} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e63e01-ec4a-57a5-86b7-843609011e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366094} {:answer/id #uuid "32c297e8-07e1-5fab-ad4c-57169fea2237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366095} {:answer/id #uuid "5466569e-0352-5327-9298-ff146556b7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5466569e-0352-5327-9298-ff146556b7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366096} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b50d6d-f46c-5fab-8128-2948e6ef2591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c06910f-cdf8-5abe-b301-896973ca0101" :question/math-academy-id "q-38919" :question/problem "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & b & -5 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x+y+z \\\\ x-y \\\\ x-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2},$ and ${b}_{3}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -3 & -1 & -10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-2$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(-2)+(-2)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124540 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "823a7d28-5a92-5901-8ee0-e5116df6766b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Image of a Vector Given the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c654010a-000f-53a3-8f7c-130cdba803bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123981} {:answer/id #uuid "d581e3dd-eeb2-5e1e-98fd-d4d976bfd07e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123982} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ee5b64-a5c3-5a85-93f6-155712809c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123983} {:answer/id #uuid "e70eabd3-9ab1-5ae3-ac24-ab47a635d42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123984} {:answer/id #uuid "14fe0cf6-65dc-52aa-a109-239dba17306e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123985}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ab85391c-787a-51d3-9471-72a3a5766ad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123980}] :question/id #uuid "c24f4b32-c910-5f42-ae2a-40df84514dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-82162" :question/problem "Let $B = {b_{1}, b_{2}, b_{3}}$ be a basis of $R^{3}$ and let $T: R^{3} → R^{3}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[T(x)]_{B}$, given that\n$[T]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $[x]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Images of the Basis Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb9e7d4-7d49-5611-aa8c-f624e6e0dc8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416371} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0f4265-777b-5a68-a83b-4d5ec07516f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416375} {:answer/id #uuid "9051dc30-494b-5b2b-98d2-22f5ecef3027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416379} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6e7a2c-0fcc-54a7-8cfc-46063d0feef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416380} {:answer/id #uuid "d806f1c8-7b38-5943-8f66-4ce22d0914ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d806f1c8-7b38-5943-8f66-4ce22d0914ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416383} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7d556e-1c97-50dc-be6c-38b9a13c9e90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "abf9f8e2-5bef-5f02-8f73-975c228317db" :question/math-academy-id "q-82461" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}.$ The matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & b & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =2{b}_{1}-{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3}, \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & ={b}_{1}+3{b}_{2}, \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =2{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}+3{b}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the coordinates of the images relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $b=3,$ $c=3$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+3+3=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56260e5b-1f89-58db-8833-b8efa77b5e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Two-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3622319-a74c-5864-a08e-fb807db69c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394389} {:answer/id #uuid "f07ffe3a-649c-5adf-8b2b-7ab2496a8fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394390} {:answer/id #uuid "3b91e62e-ada8-52a8-a4ff-c619299814db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394391} {:answer/id #uuid "b0dfeede-83bb-5d4a-9f93-28a337ca0c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394392} {:answer/id #uuid "4944cdd4-cdaf-53c7-b26b-edd99b37ad13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b91e62e-ada8-52a8-a4ff-c619299814db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394391} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a65dc9-b255-52da-b03a-40cb9a533324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9e52e1a-2cfc-5e9d-954d-1a0bc9675bab" :question/math-academy-id "q-82474" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,$ $T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351427 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56260e5b-1f89-58db-8833-b8efa77b5e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Two-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6421fbfa-a99b-5b67-ad88-93591653e262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 14 \\\\ 5 & 19\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349364} {:answer/id #uuid "786da774-d2f5-55ad-b952-5000264081bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 \\\\ 3 & 40\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349559} {:answer/id #uuid "b86285b9-bd1b-5e24-8e0f-23f2d0045479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350078} {:answer/id #uuid "c048cfb3-d0a0-5fb9-893a-c4726f8b6d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -24 \\\\ 5 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350154} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d83d05-83c2-5dd6-b651-1b166dfaee7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c048cfb3-d0a0-5fb9-893a-c4726f8b6d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -24 \\\\ 5 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350154} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a3d25e6-eb03-58c3-9578-34613afc3c3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "abe1646b-7ccf-54e1-8cd3-c4829ae02968" :question/math-academy-id "q-82476" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -11\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -24 \\\\ 5 & -11\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124541 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22ca4f81-6fec-5822-b281-5ce1e23d399e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Three-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c9e4fff-7649-56b7-8c3d-79e7b237abae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348837} {:answer/id #uuid "890ef029-0f49-5b98-bc71-bba5ccb814b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349692} {:answer/id #uuid "be9b5155-fa44-5a3c-a0fe-3af5615e1f43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350139} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ce8fd4-c220-5663-9f93-deb5265c5225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350357} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f5c2c0-e85d-5f52-8030-31304a862def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9ce8fd4-c220-5663-9f93-deb5265c5225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350357} :answer-field/id #uuid "d43dd3e3-2064-5e0a-a0e8-d374e18d14c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0147a685-a844-5e86-a953-72a451e46813" :question/math-academy-id "q-82483" :question/problem "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & b & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{3})=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=\\frac{1}{2},$ $c=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=0+\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2})=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124541 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22ca4f81-6fec-5822-b281-5ce1e23d399e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Three-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d9ee2b-0d51-5056-a43a-3b79f11f7827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348519} {:answer/id #uuid "2335ca49-a144-52ff-be29-4b560506ec3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348747} {:answer/id #uuid "509c21f8-433d-57ca-9829-87527cb30032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349176} {:answer/id #uuid "86e66244-4279-525d-b0de-1e9884ee5c39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349676} {:answer/id #uuid "a455c355-957b-5ad0-809f-690e1ed70efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a455c355-957b-5ad0-809f-690e1ed70efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349915} :answer-field/id #uuid "46e0a81a-de17-5de6-bb12-826caeb55b34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2304928b-4c80-58a1-b540-01c4b990a7c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-82497" :question/problem "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & b & -25 \\\\ a & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 2 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}y-z \\\\ x+y-z \\\\ x+y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2},$ and ${b}_{3}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 & 1 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 3 & -25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & -25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=3,$ $c=7$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=0+3+7=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124541 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22ca4f81-6fec-5822-b281-5ce1e23d399e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Three-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b74545b-9b26-59d4-acb9-27c5bfc2d8b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348544} {:answer/id #uuid "14f1e9a2-a435-5237-9e70-1c264c47563c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348625} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f63a5b-575f-5a04-87f7-e0118785f97d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350314} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2f74ba-36f2-5301-b637-5410df3c51a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350381} {:answer/id #uuid "f6bb33fb-b94e-5ee9-914e-afd4f685c109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4f63a5b-575f-5a04-87f7-e0118785f97d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350314} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc2d14c7-7aa7-5c46-94b2-8e8a9ab43990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15df9e9c-0cc2-5074-a0e8-e219fef5a119" :question/math-academy-id "q-82501" :question/problem "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 & c \\\\ -1 & b & -3 \\\\ a & 2 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}y+z \\\\ y-x \\\\ y+z-x\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2},$ and ${b}_{3}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2 & -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 & 2 & -7\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -5 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3 & 2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 & 19 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-3,$ $b=1,$ $c=19$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=(-3)+1+19=17.\n$$"}]}
